## LeetCode: Kth Largest Element in a Stream

### Approach
**Min-Heap (Priority Queue)**

- Maintain a min-heap of size `k`
- The heap stores the `k` largest elements seen so far
- The smallest element in the heap represents the current kth largest value

### Algorithm
- In the constructor, insert initial values using the same logic as `add`
- On each `add(val)`:
  - Push `val` into the heap
  - If heap size exceeds `k`, remove the smallest element
  - Return the top of the heap


class KthLargest {
public:
    int k;
    priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> heap;
    KthLargest(int k, vector<int>& nums) {
        this->k = k;
        for (int num : nums) {
            add(num);
            if(heap.size() > k)
            {
                heap.pop();
            }
        }
    }
    
    int add(int val) {
        heap.push(val);
        if(heap.size() > k)
        {
            heap.pop();
        }
        return heap.top();
    }
};

/**
 * Your KthLargest object will be instantiated and called as such:
 * KthLargest* obj = new KthLargest(k, nums);
 * int param_1 = obj->add(val);
 */
